# Scenario 'kbd_compose': メールをかく with the address picked from the address book (SELECT on the address screen: the 6-slot list with cursor moves,
# an empty slot refused, a used slot chosen), a mail title with every key (dakuten, handakuten, katakana + ウ゛, B backspace with text, title longer than the field), and a
# mail body typed on the body keyboard (kana, newline key, space key, dakuten/handakuten, katakana page, backspace) with cursor moves in the 8x12 cell grid, then saved and
# discarded (B -> dialog: いいえ, then はい) in a second attempt. Keyboard routes: tools/trace/kbdnav.py. Starts from the state left by 'kbd_abook' (two address entries,
# the reply of 'mail_inbox' in the outbox is replaced by nothing: the outbox has room). Screen names = my reading of the screenshots.
wait 400
waitstable 60 max 600
gap 30
tap A                        # title -> top menu
waitstable 60 max 600
tap A                        # top menu -> メール
waitstable 60 max 600
tap A                        # メール
waitstable 60 max 600
tap DOWN
wait 30
tap A                        # メールをかく: the outbox holds a saved mail, its check screen comes first
waitstable 60 max 600
shot saved_mail
tap RIGHT x2
wait 40
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
tap LEFT
wait 40
tap A                        # delete the saved mail: はい
waitstable 60 max 600
tap A                        # メールをかく again: now the empty address screen
waitstable 60 max 600
shot compose_intro
tap SELECT
waitstable 60 max 600
shot pick
tap DOWN
wait 60
shot pick_d1
tap DOWN x2
wait 100
tap UP
wait 60
shot pick_empty
tap A                        # A on an empty slot (refused)
waitstable 60 max 600
tap UP x2
wait 100
shot pick_top
tap A                        # A on the used slot: address goes to the address field
waitstable 60 max 600
shot addr_filled
tap START
wait 40
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
shot title_intro
tap A                        # title keyboard
waitstable 60 max 600
